# Workers Assets response headers (#1454), copied to dist/ by Vite and read by both
# edge workers (reg_webapp/edge/). Everything Vite emits under /assets/ is named by
# its content hash (scripts/smoke_build.ts checks it), so a changed file is a new
# URL and the old one never needs revalidating. index.html and the SPA fallback
# keep Workers' default `max-age=0, must-revalidate`, so a deploy shows at once.
# Footgun: the rule matches by path, so a MISSING /assets/ file gets the SPA
# fallback index.html stamped immutable too (the fallback never reaches the worker).
# A missing hashed name is never served real content later, so this only matters
# if a browser asks a colo still on the previous deploy for a new hash during
# rollout; that URL stays broken in that browser until the file's next change.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
